               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]titles[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]titles: give each LSP payload row the title ACE shows (document [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]frontmatter title, chat and artifact-file basename, bead title, agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]short name) instead of echoing the payload, so title matching and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]labelDetails/documentation affordance stop being dead code in editors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Editor payload reach and disclosed truncation[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]reach[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rank, titles[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reach: raise the per-root 200-row bound so editors see the corpus ACE [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sees, cache the inventory so the walk is not per-keystroke, and set [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]truncated_payloads so a bound that remains is disclosed rather than [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]silent.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs, release, and epic landing[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reach[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land: correct the docs/editor.md reachability claims, publish the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core release, run the editor acceptance checks, then close epic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-b3, run just symvision, and mark both plan files done.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-b3.10","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-b3.10.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e03d8b47c57db038dcf1cf07d3b193af","started_at":"2026-07-30T10:58:06.040150+00:00","state":"active"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_